          "question": "e-6559",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}-2+5\\text{i} \\\\ 5-9\\text{i} \\\\ -7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{-2+5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{5-9\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{-7+8\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-5\\text{i} \\\\ 5+9\\text{i} \\\\ -7-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
